  "scope": "Adopt five direct proofs of the exact genuine metric restriction image as Subsection27.18.1, with a section bridge, scoped historical attribution and three index entries.",
  "mathematical_boundary": "In the constructed four-point family, genuine restrictions are exactly the negative-line divisor metric times an arbitrary semipositive base metric pullback; each extends over the whole family. Least singularity is asserted only within this restriction image. No novelty, intrinsic central minimal-singularity claim, general extension theorem or original-problem closure.",
  "mathematics": {
    "fragment": "research/papers/four-point-metric-restriction-image-485.tex",
    "fragment_sha256": "d73b5344af2039f1216453a3aeec96ef471a6acfab36b4fdc9c242f93663f0a1",
    "complete_proofs": 5,
    "proof_obligations": [
      "Separate genuine central restrictions from weights identically minus infinity on X0.",
      "Use distributional Fubini to establish zero tangential Laplacian in the harmonic-slice lemma.",
      "Check upper semicontinuity, submean inequality and local integrability of disk means.",
      "Identify canonical disk means as harmonic functions.",
      "Justify decreasing disk means and the Harnack harmonic-or-minus-infinity alternative.",
      "Resolve the pencil through p4 and compute P=H-E4.",
      "Identify the three connected exceptional fibers with directions infinity, zero and one.",
      "Compute L0=O(ell)+P and degree one on ordinary pencil fibers.",
      "Factor the two central sections exactly through the divisor section and base coordinates.",
      "Check the reference metric, frame law, whole-family genuineness and curvature.",
      "Compute the variable-conic identity and nonzero determinant in the stated regime.",
      "Check simple passage through all four moving centers.",
      "Identify central conic components without extra exceptional components.",
      "Check transverse node away from all centers.",
      "Verify submersion along q minus its node, including its point on E4.",
      "Shrink the extending neighborhood using properness.",
      "Obtain genuine central curve restrictions for almost every ordinary base parameter.",
      "Obtain genuine almost-everywhere nearby compact conic restrictions by local integrability.",
      "Use positive degree-zero curvature to obtain harmonic nearby curve weights.",
      "Apply harmonic-slice persistence and exclude its degenerate alternative on good central curves.",
      "Concentrate degree-one central curve curvature at its unique node.",
      "Subtract the logarithmic atom and extend the weight difference harmonically across the node.",
      "Conclude fiberwise constancy on each good projective line.",
      "Check local sections over every base point avoid the divisor and all exceptional curves.",
      "Use the divisor section to define the correct local line-bundle frame.",
      "Construct genuine subharmonic base weights and prove agreement on overlaps from almost-everywhere equality.",
      "Check base metric transition laws.",
      "Use Fubini and canonical psh representatives to recover equality on all X0, including critical fibers.",
      "Construct the homogeneous psh weight of an arbitrary semipositive singular base metric.",
      "Check its frame law and logarithmic homogeneity.",
      "Use the compact base upper bound and the retained analytic-removability lemma at the origin.",
      "Pull back the homogeneous weight through F1,F2 and verify whole-family genuineness and exact central restriction.",
      "Prove the reference metric is least singular within extendable restrictions only."
    ],
